+    // WSA (Windows Subsystem for Android): an OPEN transition whose BLAST sync times out before the app process attaches
+    // (cold start over 5 s, e.g. a heavy React Native init) goes out empty and is aborted ("No transition roots"); the
+    // task then becomes visible without a transition, FreeformTaskTransitionObserver never calls onTaskOpening, and
+    // nobody positions or crops the task leash. It stays at (0, 0): the window is drawn in its own Windows window all
+    // the same, but input (host mouse and adb alike) is dispatched by the leash geometry and misses it. So a while after
+    // a task turns visible, do what the opening would have done: the decoration (a plain relayout if there is one) and
+    // the leash position and crop the transition sets for freeform tasks.
+    private static final long WSA_VISIBLE_SETTLE_MS = 500;
+    // Created on first use, on the shell main thread the task callbacks come on: the listener itself is constructed
+    // on the SystemUI main thread, and a decoration opened from there would be touched from two threads.
+    private Handler mWsaHandler;
